# gdd/Scenarios.md: director skeleton. Pick runs once at on_startup in HAI
# scope; the ladder tick runs monthly under `if tag(HAI)`.
# State (globals, all 0 until picked):
#   sandbox_scenario: 0 none, 1 axis_expansion, 2 soviet_expansion,
#     3 japanese_expansion, 4 italian_expansion, 5 fascist_britain,
#     6 red_america, 7 napoleonic_france, 8 habsburg_restoration
#   sandbox_scenario_phase: 0 smolder, 1 crises, 2 peak, 3 ended
#   sandbox_scenario_pin: 0 random, 1 pinned to the picked arc
#   sandbox_derailed_arcs[]: ids that derailed this session (never repicked)

# Target variants for the active arc (gdd/Scenarios Catalog.md). HSL cannot
# hold tags in variables, so the chosen pair is written straight into the
# persistent sandbox_targets[] array. Variant is a global string used for
# logging and data. Variant A is the arc's historical default; variant B is
# the catalog alt. The 50/50 roll happens in the picker before calling this.
sandbox_set_targets():
  global.&sandbox_targets[].clear()
  if global.sandbox_scenario == 1:
    if global.sandbox_target_variant == a:
      global.&sandbox_targets[].add(CZE)
